    "evidence_text": "RNase H and Postreplication Repair Protect Cells from Ribonucleotides Incorporated in DNA\n\nMisincorporation is limited by the selectivity of DNA replicases.\n\nThe screen was based on visual readouts, using inducible, fluorescent ribosomal proteins as reporters.\n\nRibosome Profiling Provides Evidence that Large Noncoding RNAs Do Not Encode Proteins\n\nLarge noncoding RNAs are emerging as an important component in cellular regulation.\n\nmiRNA-dependent gene silencing involving Ago2-mediated cleavage of a circular antisense RNA.\n\nDecoding Mammalian Ribosome-mRNA States by Translational GTPase Complexes\n\nLincRNA-p21 suppresses target mRNA translation.\n\nExpression of Versican 3\u2032-Untranslated Region Modulates Endogenous MicroRNA Functions\n\nThe decrease in miRNA activity consequently translated into differences in tumor growth.\n\nThis non-coding component of mRNA may be used retrospectively to modulate miRNA activities.\n\nUV crosslinking revealed multiple Rat1-binding sites across the pre-rRNA, consistent with its known functions.\n\nITS2 was reported to undergo structural remodelling.\n\nChaperoning 5S RNA assembly.\n\nThe complexity of human ribosome biogenesis revealed by systematic nucleolar screening of Pre-rRNA processing factors.",
